amily of instruments'. Qmin at measuring ratio (MR) 1:30 applies for pressures 0–101 bar(g); Qmin at MR 1:50 applies for 4–101 bar(g). Bearing dimensions are inside diameter x outside diameter x width in mm, listed for standard and optional bearings (front and rear), valid for 0–101 bar(g). Each instrument type (FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc; FMT-S, FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc) with a given DN body/cartridge combination is certified in three G-value variants. Number of drums is given as before/after the decimal comma; control element value 0.2. Data under 1.2 Essential characteristics (flows), 1.4 Conditional parts (drums, control element), 1.1 Essential parts (blade angle/qty, bearings).\"\n\ntype_level characteristics:\n- number_of_drums_before_comma: {value: 8, unit_symbol: null}\n- number_of_drums_after_comma: {value: 0, unit_symbol: null}\n- control_element: {value: 0.2, unit_symbol: \"m³/lh\"}\n- blade_quantity: {value: 24, unit_symbol: null}\n\nHmm, \"Number of drums Before and after comma\" — \"8 / 0\": 8 drums before comma, 0 after. Yes.\n\nNow, the certificate scheme: number \"R137/2012-B-NL1-18.05\" → scheme \"B\". Yes.\n\npage_total: 5 (from \"Page 4 of 5\").\n\nLet me now write out all 42 rows carefully, cross-checking against the markdown.\n\nMarkdown rows in order:\n\n1. Type \"FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc\" rowspan, DN body 200, DN cartr 250, drums \"8 / 0\", control \"0,2\", bearings rowspan: 10x26x8, 6x16x5, 12x28x8, 6x19x6.\n   - R1: 1000, 1600, 320, 50, 32, 45, 24\n   - R2: 1600, 2500, 500, 80, 50, 45 / 30, 24\n   - R3: 2500, 4000, 800, 125, 80, 30, 24\n\n2. \"FMT-S, FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc\", 250, 250, drums 8/0, control 0,2, bearings 10x26x8, 6x16x5, 12x28x8, 6x19x6.\n   - R1: 1000, 1600, 320, 50, 32, 45, 24\n   - R2: 1600, 2500, 500, 80, 50, 45 / 30, 24\n   - R3: 2500, 4000, 800, 125, 80, 30, 24\n\n3. \"FMT-Lx or FMT-Dc\", 250, 300, 8/0, 0,2, bearings 12x28x8, 6x19x6, 17x40x12, 8x22x7.\n   - R1: 1600, 2500, 500, 80, 50, 45, 24\n   - R2: 2500, 4000, 800, 125, 80, 45 / 30, 24\n   - R3: 4